# Frontend settings. Copy to web/.env.local (gitignored) and edit.
#
# Only NEXT_PUBLIC_* values reach the browser — they are inlined at BUILD time, so a
# change needs a dev-server restart or a rebuild. Backend settings (database, API keys)
# live in core/.env and are deliberately NOT loaded here: the web process has no need
# for a database password, and keeping them apart means a NEXT_PUBLIC_ typo cannot turn
# a credential into a public one.

# Hide the site-wide banner on this machine. Opt-OUT: a deployment that never sets it
# still shows the banner, so a demo site cannot silently present generated figures as
# real. See web/src/config/banner.ts for the message itself.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_BANNER_DISABLED=true

# The Setup link is NOT configured here. It appears wherever the API serves the setup
# routes, which is governed by SETUP_ENABLED in core/.env — one setting for both, so the
# link and the routes cannot disagree.
